- Retrieve: GET /MedicationRequest?patient=Patient/{MRN}&status=active
- For each MedicationRequest:
  - Name/strength: from medicationCodeableConcept.text or coding.display; strength may be in text; if needed and available, resolve the referenced Medication resource for form/ingredient.
  - Route: dosageInstruction.route.coding/display or text parsing (e.g., “po,” “by mouth,” “ophthalmic”).
  - Frequency: dosageInstruction.timing.repeat (frequency, period, periodUnit); handle ranges (frequencyMax) and PRN.
  - Formulation: if present (e.g., “tablet,” “capsule”); otherwise infer from text.
  - Ingredient: prefer ingredient-level coding if present (e.g., RxNorm ingredient); otherwise normalize generic name (strip strength/form).

- Grouping and flags:
  - Group by ingredient + formulation + route.
  - Flag potential duplicate therapy when multiple active items share the same ingredient (and route) concurrently; note brand/generic duplicates and combo products that include the same ingredient.

- Daily pill burden (oral tablets/capsules only):
  - Include only items with oral route and tablet/capsule formulation.
  - Compute doses/day from timing:
    - If frequency/periodUnit = d, doses/day = frequency.
    - If periodUnit ≠ d (e.g., h, wk), convert to per-day.
    - If ranges or PRN: report as a range (e.g., 1–2/day) or exclude PRN from baseline and footnote.
  - Sum across all qualifying meds to get total daily oral pill count.
  - List all non-oral items separately (topicals, inhalers, injectables, ophthalmic/otic, nasal, transdermal, buccal/sublingual, rectal, etc.) with name, strength, route, frequency.

- Suggested output structure (template):
  - Oral tablets/capsules (grouped by ingredient/formulation/route)
    - Ingredient: [name]
      - [Brand/Generic name] [strength], [route], [frequency] — [tablet/capsule]
      - ...
  - Non-oral items
    - [Name] [strength], [route], [frequency] — [form]
  - Potential duplicate therapies (by ingredient)
    - [Ingredient]: [Medication A], [Medication B]
  - Total daily oral pill count: [N] (note assumptions: PRN handling, ranges, unknowns)

