fy current clinical intent).\n- Mirtazapine 45 mg PO tablets (oral solid)\n  - QHS. Pill burden: 1 tab/day.\n- Other non-oral, non-daily/procedural or one-time items\n  - Heparin, porcine (PF) 5,000 Units/0.5 mL SC inj (Pre-Op once)\n  - Gadobutrol IV contrast (Radiology) once\n  - Piperacillin-tazobactam IV q8h (two product variants)\n\nComputed daily pill burden (solid oral dosage units only)\n- Counted once per ingredient despite duplicate orders:\n  - Tacrolimus: ~1 cap/day (pending reconciliation due to conflicting schedules)\n  - Valganciclovir: 1 tab/day\n  - Ferrous sulfate: 1 tab/day\n  - Diltiazem: 1 cap/day\n  - Levofloxacin: 1 tab/day\n  - Mirtazapine: 1 tab/day\n- Total estimated solid oral units per day: 6\nNotes on other routes/forms (not included in pill count)\n- Insulin NPH: approximately 1 SC injection/day (duplicates present)\n- Insulin lispro sliding-scale: variable SC injections (meals/bedtime or Q6H NPO); multiple concurrent scales present\u2014potential duplication; do not sum.\n- Apheresis-related heparin and methoxsalen: per-session, not daily pills.\n\nPotential duplicates by ingredient flagged\n- Heparin (apheresis solutions): multiple active orders\n- Methoxsalen (inj solution): multiple active orders\n- Insulin lispro (multiple scale regimens): overlapping active orders\n- Insulin NPH (multiple daily orders/doses)\n- Tacrolimus 0.5 mg PO caps (several schedules)\n- Valganciclovir 450 mg PO tabs (more than one QAM order)\n- Diltiazem HCl 90 mg PO CP12 (more than one DAILY order)\n\nProposed Observation to create (for your review)\n- Patient: Jonathan Jackson (MRN S1733937, DOB 1984-11-03)\n- Resource: Observation\n- status: final\n- code.text: Medication reconciliation summary\n- subject.reference: Patient/S1733937\n- valueString narrative (to be saved): the grouped medication summary above, including the computed daily pill burden (solid oral units/day = 6) and the flagged potential duplicates.\n\nAbout timestamps and next step\n- Per p