      "content": "Thanks. I\u2019m operating as a clinical workflow assistant using the EMR/FHIR tools only.\n\nPatient confirmed for this session:\n- Victoria Owens (MRN S3236936, DOB 2002-06-07)\n\nPart 1) Active MedicationRequest retrieval and analysis\n- EMR-retrieved facts (FHIR MedicationRequest, status=active, subject=Patient/S3236936):\n  - A large number of active medication orders were returned (multiple continuous infusions, scheduled enteral meds, and many \u201conce\u201d orders). Examples include FUROSEMIDE (several IV push orders, one continuous IV infusion), multiple sedative/analgesic infusions (propofol, dexmedetomidine, hydromorphone, midazolam), antibiotics (piperacillin\u2013tazobactam, meropenem, ertapenem), and numerous enteral medications (acetaminophen in multiple forms, guanfacine, pregabalin, lactulose, polyethylene glycol, senna/sennosides, famotidine), among others. AuthoredOn dates range from 2023-10-28 to 2023-11-13; all are currently marked active in the EMR.\n\nGrouped summary by ingredient, pharmaceutical form, and route (with duplicate flags)\n- FUROSEMIDE (duplicate flag: YES)\n  - IV inj soln (Once 10 mg; Once 20 mg; Once 40 mg; Once 60 mg; plus TID 60 mg)\n  - IV infusion (Continuous)\n  - Daily administration burden: 3/day (from the TID IV push order) + 1 continuous infusion; \u201cOnce\u201d doses are one-time.\n- ACETAMINOPHEN (duplicate flag: YES)\n  - PO tablets via feeding tube (500 mg Q6H; 325 mg Q6H; additional 500 mg Q6H orders)\n  - PO solution (650 mg/20.3 mL) Q6H oral; several one-time doses also present\n  - Daily administration burden: 5 concurrent Q6H orders \u2192 20 administrations/day\n- DEXMEDETOMIDINE (duplicate flag: YES)\n  - IV infusion (multiple concurrent continuous orders documented)\n  - Daily administration burden: continuous infusions x ~11 (no discrete daily count)\n- MIDAZOLAM (duplicate flag: YES)\n  - IV infusion (Continuous) x ~3\n  - IV bolus (Once) x several; PO syrup (Once)\n  - Daily administration burden: continuous x ~3; bolus orders are one-time\n- HYDROMORPHONE (duplicate flag: YES)\n  - IV infusion (Continuous) x ~5\n  - IV bolus (Once)\n  - Daily administration burden: continuous x ~5\n- NOREPINEPHRINE (duplicate flag: YES)\n  - IV infusion (Continuous) x ~3\n  - Concentrated IV infusion (Continuous) x 1\n  - Daily administration burden: continuous x ~4\n- PROPOFOL (duplicate flag: YES)\n  - IV infusion (Continuous) x ~8\n  - IV injection (Once) x 2\n  - Daily administration burden: continuous x ~8\n- KETAMINE (duplicate flag: YES)\n  - IV infusion (Continuous) x 2\n  - IV bolus (Once) x 1\n  - Daily administration burden: continuous x 2\n- NITRIC OXIDE (duplicate flag: YES)\n  - Inhalation (Continuous) x 2\n- CISATRACURIUM (duplicate flag: YES)\n  - IV infusion (Continuous) x 1\n  - IV bolus (Once) x 1\n- GUANFACINE (duplicate flag: YES)\n  - PO/Feeding tube tablets (TID 2 mg; TID 0.5 mg)\n  - Daily administration burden: 6/day\n- POLYETHYLENE GLYCOL 3350 (duplicate flag: YES)\n  - PO/Feeding tube packets (BID x 2 orders; DAILY x 2 orders)\n  - Daily administration burden: 6/day\n- SENNA/SENNOSIDES (duplicate flag: YES)\n  - Syrup via feeding tube (BID x 2; DAILY x 1)\n  - Tablets via feeding tube (BID x 1; DAILY x 1)\n  - Daily administration burden: 8/day\n- LACTULOSE (duplicate flag: YES)\n  - PO/Feeding tube solution (DAILY x 1; TID x 1)\n  - Daily administration burden: 4/day\n- FAMOTIDINE (duplicate flag: YES)\n  - PO/Feeding tube suspension or tablets (BID x 2)\n  - Daily administration burden: 4/day\n- LEVETIRACETAM (duplicate flag: YES)\n  - IV (Q12H) and IV (Q15 MIN), plus PO solution (QAM)\n  - Daily administration burden: ~99/day (2/day from IV Q12H + 96/day from IV Q15 MIN + 1/day PO); very likely unintended duplication\n- OXCARBAZEPINE (duplicate flag: YES)\n  - PO tablets (Q8H; BID) and PO suspension (BID)\n  - Daily administration burden: 7/day\n- POTASSIUM CHLORIDE (duplicate flag: YES)\n  - IV (Q1H 20 mEq; Once 20 mEq), PO once