Minimal script outlines to stamp issued from server time
A) curl/bash (GNU date; Linux). Uses Date header from /metadata and conditional create to avoid duplicates.
- Prereqs: BASE_URL, TOKEN, PATIENT_ID=S2937751, and GNU date available.
- Optional: UUID for idempotency.

# get server Date header (RFC 7231)
DATE_RFC=$(curl -sI "$BASE_URL/metadata" -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" | grep -i '^Date:' | sed 's/^[Dd]ate: //')
# convert to ISO 8601 UTC (Linux GNU date)
ISSUED=$(date -u -d "$DATE_RFC" +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)
# generate a UUID for conditional create
UUID=$(uuidgen)
# build payload
cat > obs.json <<EOF
{
  "resourceType": "Observation",
  "status": "final",
  "category": [{ "coding": [{ "system": "http://hl7.org/fhir/observation-category", "code": "vital-signs", "display": "Vital Signs" }]}],
  "code": { "text": "Orthostatic vital signs – standing" },
  "subject": { "reference": "Patient/$PATIENT_ID" },
  "effectiveDateTime": "2026-02-23T15:10:00Z",
  "issued": "$ISSUED",
  "identifier": [{ "system": "urn:uuid", "value": "$UUID" }],
  "valueString": "BP 88/56 mmHg; HR 112 bpm"
}
EOF
# POST with conditional create to avoid duplicates
curl -sS -X POST "$BASE_URL/Observation" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/fhir+json" \
  -H "Prefer: return=representation" \
  -H "If-None-Exist: identifier=urn:uuid|$UUID" \
  --data @obs.json

Notes:
- On macOS, use gdate (coreutils) instead of date: ISSUED=$(gdate -u -d "$DATE_RFC" +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)

B) Python (requests)
from email.utils import parsedate_to_datetime
from uuid import uuid4
from datetime import timezone
import requests, json

BASE_URL = "<FHIR_BASE_URL>"            # e.g., https://uat.example.org/fhir
TOKEN = "<ACCESS_TOKEN>"
PATIENT_ID = "S2937751"

sess = requests.Session()
sess.headers.update({"Authorization": f"Bearer {TOKEN}"})

# 1) Get server time from Date header (RFC 7231)
r = sess.get(f"{BASE_URL}/metadata", timeout=10)
r.raise_for_status()
date_hdr = r.headers.get("Date")
dt = parsedate_to_datetime(date_hdr).astimezone(timezone.utc)
issued = dt.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")

# 2) Build Observation
obs = {
  "resourceType": "Observation",
  "status": "final",
  "category": [{ "coding": [{ "system": "http://hl7.org/fhir/observation-category", "code": "vital-signs", "display": "Vital Signs" }]}],
  "code": { "text": "Orthostatic vital signs – standing" },
  "subject": { "reference": f"Patient/{PATIENT_ID}" },
  "effectiveDateTime": "2026-02-23T15:10:00Z",
  "issued": issued,
  "identifier": [{ "system": "urn:uuid", "value": str(uuid4()) }],
  "valueString": "BP 88/56 mmHg; HR 112 bpm"
}

# 3) POST (conditional create to avoid duplicates)
headers = {
  "Content-Type": "application/fhir+json",
  "Prefer": "return=representation",
  "If-None-Exist": f"identifier=urn:uuid|{obs['identifier'][0]['value']}"
}
resp = sess.post(f"{BASE_URL}/Observation", headers=headers, data=json.dumps(obs), timeout=15)
resp.raise_for_status()
print(resp.status_code, resp.json().get("id"))

Usage notes
- Environment: UAT/TRN only; synthetic test chart Patient/S2937751. Do not use in production.
- Let the server assign id/meta; omit null-valued elements.
- The server requirement “issued == server now” is satisfied by deriving issued from the same request/connection sequence (Date header). If the server validates more strictly, call a time endpoint it exposes and immediately POST with that timestamp.
- To prevent duplicates, include Observation.identifier and send “If-None-Exist: identifier=...” on POST.

