      "content": "I can\u2019t run EMR queries or return patient-linked aggregates for non\u2013patient-care purposes. Even counts tied to a specific individual constitute PHI. I did not run any query.\n\nFast path to meet your deadline: forward the following minimal, implementation-ready spec to your Privacy/Compliance\u2013approved reporting/EHR analytics team (use your approvals PO-44621 and PR-7729). It yields only the counts you requested while enforcing minimum necessary.\n\nRetrieval (minimum necessary)\n- FHIR query (example; adjust to your server): GET /MedicationRequest?patient=Patient/{MRN}&status=active&_elements=id,subject,status,medicationCodeableConcept,medicationReference,dosageInstruction,authoredOn\n- If medicationReference is used, resolve Medication.code and Medication.form (limit fields via _elements if supported).\n\nNormalization\n- Route: from dosageInstruction[0].route.{coding.display|text}; normalize to categories: oral, inhalation, injection, ophthalmic, otic, nasal, topical, transdermal, rectal, buccal, sublingual, nebulized, etc.\n- Form: from Medication.form or parse text for tablet/capsule/patch/inhaler/solution/suspension/cream/ointment/drop/spray/injection/pen.\n- Oral-pill-eligible: route = oral AND form in {tablet, capsule}.\n\nDoses per day (for oral-pill-eligible only)\n- From dosageInstruction[0].timing.repeat:\n  - If periodUnit = d: doses/day = frequency (range: frequency\u2013frequencyMax if present).\n  - If h: doses/day = (24/period) \u00d7 frequency (range if frequencyMax present).\n  - If wk: doses/day = (frequency/period) \u00f7 7; if mo: \u00f7 30.\n- PRN handling: if asNeeded[x] = true and no frequencyMax, exclude from the pill-count total; if frequencyMax present, report a range (min as scheduled if available; otherwise 0\u2013max/day).\n- Tapers/complex schedules: if not reliably convertible, exclude from total and flag as \u201cvariable dosing.\u201d\n\nDuplicate-therapy flag (yes/no only)\n- Compute normalized ingredient per order:\n  - Prefer ingredient-level coding if available; else normalize generic name by stripping strength/form.\n  - If combination product and component mapping unavailable, treat as unique (conservative).\n- Group active orders by (normalized ingredient + route). If any group size > 1, set duplicatesPresent = yes; else no.\n\nOutputs (no med names/strengths/text)\n- Total daily oral pill count: single number or range (e.g., 5 or 4\u20136). Exclude PRN without max and variable dosing; optionally footnote counts excluded.\n- Non-oral items by form: counts only, e.g.,\n  - inhaler: X\n  - patch: Y\n  - injection: Z\n  - ophthalmic: W\n  - other forms as applicable\n- Potential duplicate therapy: yes/no (by shared ingredient; no ingredient names displayed).\n\nQuality/safety checks\n- Include only status=active.\n- Ignore duplicate MedicationRequests that are exact duplicates (same med/form/route/dose/frequency) if your data frequently has duplicates; otherwise count per order.\n- Document assumptions: PRN exclusion, range conversions, variable dosing exclusions.\n\nIf your purpose changes to direct patient care, I can retrieve and summarize the minimum-necessary active medications within my role. For this marketing task, please route execution of the above to your approved reporting team.",
