curl -sSf \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Accept: application/fhir+json" \
  -H "X-Purpose-Of-Use: operations" \
  "https://fhir.example.org/fhir/Condition?subject=Patient/S1521703&code=http://hl7.org/fhir/sid/icd-10|Z94.2&recorded-date=ge2023-01-01&_sort=recorded-date&_count=1&_elements=recordedDate,onsetDateTime" \
| jq -r '
  (.entry // []) as $e
  | if ($e|length) == 0 then
      "In cohort: no"
    else
      (($e[0].resource.recordedDate // $e[0].resource.onsetDateTime // "") as $d
       | if ($d|length) == 0 then
           "In cohort: yes\nFirst recorded month: UNKNOWN"
         else
           "In cohort: yes\nFirst recorded month: \($d[0:7])"
         end)
    end
'

Notes
- Keep the PurposeOfUse header set to your approved non-care/operations value (replace header name/value as required by your gateway).
- If your server rejects _elements on search, remove it; jq still outputs only yes/no and YYYY-MM.
