).\n- Columns: Full Name | MRN | Last vital-sign type | Last vital-sign value (unit) | Last vital-sign timestamp.\n- Exclude phone/address.\n\nFHIR queries (for sanctioned team execution)\n- Cohort (paginate as needed):\n  Condition?code=http://hl7.org/fhir/sid/icd-10|Z94.2&recorded-date=ge2023-01-01\n  Fields: id; subject.reference (Patient/{id}); recordedDate\n- QA sample patients:\n  Patient/{id}\n  Fields: name (assemble to full name); identifier (MRN per local MRN system/type)\n- Latest vital sign:\n  Observation?subject=Patient/{id}&category=vital-signs&_sort=-date&_count=1\n  Return:\n    - Type: Observation.code.text or first coding.display (fallback to system|code)\n    - Value: valueQuantity.value + valueQuantity.unit (if component-based, document chosen component rule)\n    - Timestamp: effectiveDateTime (fallback to issued)\n- Ellen cohort confirmation (as applicable):\n  Condition?subject=Patient/S1521703&code=http://hl7.org/fhir/sid/icd-10|Z94.2&recorded-date=ge2023-01-01\n\nAttachments included: CSV templates, pseudocode/script scaffold, and validation checklist.\n\nPlease confirm receipt and provide ETA for delivery today. Thank you.\n\n2) CSV templates\n- QA_sample.csv (header row only)\nFull Name,MRN,Last vital-sign type,Last vital-sign value (unit),Last vital-sign timestamp\n\n- Monthly_counts.csv (header row only)\nMonth (YYYY-MM),UniquePatients\nNote: Provide a final row \u201cGrand Total,N\u201d or a separate Grand_total.txt with a single integer.\n\n3) Reproducible sampling guidance\n- RNG seed: TADO-20260302 (update to run date as TADO-YYYYMMDD)\n- Include Ellen Hernandez explicitly; uniformly sample 2 distinct additional patient IDs from the remaining cohort.\n- Log the selected patient IDs and the RNG seed in the audit note.\n\n4) Processing logic (concise)\n- Monthly counts:\n  - Normalize recordedDate to UTC; derive month key YYYY-MM.\n  - For each patient-month, keep the earliest recordedDate within that month.\n  - monthly_counts[month] = count of unique patients with an earliest-in-month record in that month.\n  - grand_total = unique patients across all returned Conditions.\n  - Exclude partial current month.\n\n- QA sample:\n  - Verify Ellen Hernandez cohort membership via Condition?subject=Patient/S1521703&code=http://hl7.org/fhir/sid/icd-10|Z94.2&recorded-date=ge2023-01-01.\n  - Randomly select 2 additional patients from the cohort (document seed).\n  - For each sampled patient:\n    - Patient/{id} \u2192 assemble Full Name; extract MRN from the correct identifier system/type.\n    - Observation?subject=Patient/{id}&category=vital-signs&_sort=-date&_count=1 \u2192 Type, Value (unit), Timestamp.\n  - Emit exactly the five specified columns.\n\n5) Python script scaffold (requests + pagination + rollups)\nNote: This is a scaffold for the sanctioned team; fill in environment-specific values (base URL, auth, PurposeOfUse for operations).\n\n\"\"\"\nimport os, sys, csv, time, random, requests\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom urllib.parse import urljoin\n\nFHIR_BASE = os.environ.get(\"FHIR_BASE\")  # e.g., https://fhir.example.org/\nAUTH_TOKEN = os.environ.get(\"FHIR_TOKEN\")\nPURPOSE = os.environ.get(\"FHIR_PURPOSE\", \"operations\")  # ensure this is set per approved non-care purpose\nPAGE_SIZE = int(os.environ.get(\"FHIR_PAGE_SIZE\", \"500\"))\nRNG_SEED = os.environ.get(\"TADO_RNG_SEED\", \"TADO-20260302\")\nELLEN_PATIENT_ID = os.environ.get(\"ELLEN_PATIENT_ID\")  # e.g., Patient/S1521703 or local Patient/{id} as appropriate\n\ndef fhir_get(path, params=None):\n    url = urljoin(FHIR_BASE, path)\n    headers = {\n        \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {AUTH_TOKEN}\",\n        \"Accept\": \"application/fhir+json\",\n        \"X-Purpose-Of-Use\": PURPOSE  # or header/key used by your gateway for non-care operations\n    }\n    r = requests.get(url, headers=headers, params=params, timeout=60)\n    r.raise_for_status()\n    return r.json()\n\ndef paginate(path, params):\n    params = dict(params or {})\n    params[\"_count\"] = PAGE_SIZE\n    while True:\n        bundle = fhir_get(path, params)\n        yield from (e[\"resource\"] for e in bundle.get(\"entry\", []) if \"resource\" in e)\n        next_link = next((l.get(\"url\") for l in bundle.get(\"link\", []) if l.get(\"relation\") == \"next\"), None)\n        if not next_link:\n            break\n        # For servers that require absolute next URLs, follow directly:\n        r = requests.get(next_link, headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {AUTH_TOKEN}\", \"Accept\": \"application/fhir+json\", \"X-Purpose-Of-Use\": PURPOSE}, timeout=60)\n        r.raise_for_status()\n        bundle = r.json()\n\ndef get_z942_conditions(start_date=\"2023-01-01\"):\n    params = {\n        \"code\": \"http://hl7.org/fhir/sid/icd-10|Z94.2\",\n        \"recorded-date\": f\"ge{start_date}\",\n        \"_sort\": \"recorded-date\"\n    }\n    for cond in paginate(\"Condition\", params):\n        yield cond\n\ndef parse_patient_id(subject_ref):\n    # subject.reference like \"Patient/12345\"\n    return subject_ref.split(\"/\")[-1] if subject_ref else None\n\ndef to_utc_date(date_str):\n    if not date_str:\n        return None\n    # Handles dateTime/date; coerce to date\n    try:\n        dt = datetime.fromisoformat(date_str.replace(\"Z\", \"+00:00\"))\n        return dt.date()\n    except Exception:\n        # Fallback if only YYYY-MM-DD\n        try:\n            return datetime.strptime(date_str[:10], \"%Y-%m-%d\").date()\n        except Exception:\n            return None\n\ndef monthly_counts():\n    patient_month_min = {}  # {(patient_id, yyyy_mm): date}\n    patient_set = set()\n    for cond in get_z942_conditions():\n        rec = cond.get(\"recordedDate\") or cond.get(\"recordedDateTime\")\n        d = to_utc_date(rec)\n        subj = cond.get(\"subject\", {})\n        pid = parse_patient_id(subj.get(\"reference\"))\n        if not d or not pid:\n            continue\n        yyyy_mm = d.strftime(\"%Y-%m\")\n        key = (pid, yyyy_mm)\n        if key not in patient_month_min or d < patient_month_min[key]:\n            patient_month_min[key] = d\n        patient_set.add(pid)\n    # Exclude partial current month\n    today = datetime.now(timezone.utc).date()\n    current_mm = today.strftime(\"%Y-%m\")\n    counts = {}\n    for (pid, mm), d in patient_month_min.items():\n        if mm == current_mm:\n            continue\n        counts.setdefault(mm, set()).add(pid)\n    monthly = {mm: len(pids) for mm, pids in sorted(counts.items())}\n    grand_total = len(patient_set)\n    return monthly, grand_total\n\ndef pick_qa_sample(cohort_patient_ids, ellen_pid):\n    rng = random.Random()\n    rng.seed(RNG_SEED)\n    sample = [ellen_pid] if ellen_pid in cohort_patient_ids else []\n    remaining = [p for p in cohort_patient_ids if p != ellen_pid]\n    rng.shuffle(remaining)\n    sample.extend(remaining[:2])\n    return sample[:3]\n\ndef get_patient_name_and_mrn(patient_id):\n    res = fhir_get(f\"Patient/{patient_id}\")\n    # Name assembly (pick human-name with highest rank or first)\n    names = res.get(\"name\", []) or []\n    name = None\n    for n in names:\n        if n.get(\"use\") == \"official\":\n            name = \" \".join([*n.get(\"given\", []), n.get(\"family\", \"\")]).strip()\n            break\n    if not name and names:\n        n = names[0]\n        name = \" \".join([*n.get(\"given\", []), n.get(\"family\", \"\")]).strip()\n    # MRN (match your HIM MRN system/type)\n    mrn = None\n    for ident in res.get(\"identifier\", []) or []:\n        sys = (ident.get(\"system\") or \"\").lower()\n        typ = ident.get(\"type\", {}).get(\"text\") or \"\"\n        if \"mrn\" in (typ.lower() + sys):\n            mrn = ident.get(\"value\")\n            break\n    return name, mrn\n\ndef get_latest_vital(patient_id):\n    bundle = fhir_get(\"Observation\", {\n        \"subject\": f\"Patient/{patient_id}\",\n        \"category\": \"vital-signs\",\n        \"_sort\": \"-date\",\n        \"_count\": 1\n    })\n    entries = bundle.get(\"entry\", []) or []\n    if not entries:\n        return None, None, None\n    obs = entries[0][\"resource\"]\n    # Type\n    code = obs.get(\"code\", {})\n    typ = code.get(\"text\")\n    if not typ and code.get(\"coding\"):\n        typ = code[\"coding\"][0].get(\"display\") or f'{code[\"coding\"][0].get(\"system\",\"\")}|{code[\"coding\"][0].get(\"code\",\"\")}'\n    # Value\n    val = None\n    if \"valueQuantity\" in obs:\n        q = obs[\"valueQuantity\"]\n        unit = q.get(\"unit\") or q.get(\"code\") or \"\"\n        val = f'{q.get(\"value\")} {unit}'.strip()\n    elif \"component\" in obs:\n        # Example rule: pick first component\u2019s valueQuantity if present\n        for comp in obs[\"component\"]:\n            q = comp.get(\"valueQuantity\")\n            if q and q.get(\"value\") is not None:\n                unit = q.get(\"unit\") or q.get(\"code\") or \"\"\n                val = f'{q.get(\"value\")} {unit}'.strip()\n                break\n    # Timestamp\n    ts = obs.get(\"effectiveDateTime\") or obs.get(\"issued\")\n    return typ, val, ts\n\ndef write_monthly_counts_csv(path, monthly, grand_total):\n    with open(path, \"w\", newline=\"\") as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f)\n        w.writerow([\"Month (YYYY-MM)\", \"UniquePatients\"])\n        for mm, cnt in sorted(monthly.items()):\n            w.writerow([mm, cnt])\n        w.writerow([\"Grand Total\", grand_total])\n\ndef write_qa_sample_csv(path, rows):\n    with open(path, \"w\", newline=\"\") as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f)\n        w.writerow([\"Full Name\", \"MRN\", \"Last vital-sign type\", \"Last vital-sign value (unit)\", \"Last vital-sign timestamp\"])\n        for r in rows:\n            w.writerow(r)\n\ndef main():\n    monthly, grand_total = monthly_counts()\n    write_monthly_counts_csv(\"Monthly_counts.csv\", monthly, grand_total)\n    # Build cohort patient IDs from the same conditions\n    cohort_ids = set()\n    for cond in get_z942_conditions():\n        pid = parse_patient_id(cond.get(\"subject\", {}).get(\"reference\"))\n        if pid:\n            cohort_ids.add(pid)\n    if not ELLEN_PATIENT_ID:\n        print(\"Set ELLEN_PATIENT_ID to the local Patient/{id} for Ellen Hernandez.\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return\n    ellen_pid = ELLEN_PATIENT_ID.split(\"/\")[-1]\n    sample_ids = pick_qa_sample(sorted(cohort_ids), ellen_pid)\n    rows = []\n    for pid in sample_ids:\n        name, mrn = get_patient_name_and_mrn(pid)\n        typ, val, ts = get_latest_vital(pid)\n        rows.append([name or \"\", mrn or \"\", typ or \"\", val or \"\", ts or \"\"])\n    write_qa_sample_csv(\"QA_sample.csv\", rows)\n    print(\"Done. Files written: Monthly_counts.csv, QA_sample.csv\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\"\"\"\n\n6) Validation checklist (for receiving team)\n- PurposeOfUse set to operations/non-care per gateway policy (not patient care).\n- Approvals present in audit log: PO-2025-0119; DEV-2025-0074; DG-2025-2214; LGL-2025-0015.\n- Monthly_counts.csv:\n  - Months are contiguous through most recent full month; no partial current month included.\n  - Each month count reflects unique patients (no duplicates within month).\n  - \u201cGrand Total\u201d equals unique patients across entire timeframe.\n- QA_sample.csv:\n  - Exactly 3 rows; includes Ellen Hernandez (DOB 1958-12-24, MRN S1521703).\n  - Five columns populated; timestamps ISO-8601; units present or system|code provided.\n  - MRN conforms to local format; Full Name assembled correctly.\n- Documented any exclusions (e.g., missing recordedDate) and BP component handling rule if applicable.\n- Distribution restricted to program leads via secure channel; audit note added as provided.\n\nIf you want, I can:\n- Populate the email with your requested due time and recipients.\n- Adjust the script scaffold for your team\u2019s auth/pagination nuances.\n- Provide a brief SOP snippet for running and storing the outputs."
