ion/commit, RNG seed, run timestamp, row counts, exclusions) to a text or JSON log alongside outputs.\n- Error handling and retries:\n  - Add bounded retries (e.g., 3 tries with exponential backoff) for transient 429/5xx responses on searches.\n- Security/POU header:\n  - Keep the purpose header name configurable (env var), since different gateways use different header keys.\n\nMinimal code adjustments (drop-in)\n- Observation latest-vital call params: include status=final.\n- Add optional _elements where supported.\n- Add run metadata file creation.\n\nExample param additions (conceptual; adapt to your environment)\n- Condition search params:\n  { \"code\": \"http://hl7.org/fhir/sid/icd-10|Z94.2\", \"recorded-date\": \"ge2023-01-01\", \"_sort\": \"recorded-date\", \"_elements\": \"id,subject,recordedDate\" }\n- Observation search params:\n  { \"subject\": \"Patient/{id}\", \"category\": \"vital-signs\", \"status\": \"final\", \"_sort\": \"-date\", \"_count\": 1, \"_elements\": \"id,code,valueQuantity,component,effectiveDateTime,issued,category,status\" }\n- Patient read:\n  Patient/{id}?_elements=name,identifier\n\nShort SOP for sanctioned team\n- PurposeOfUse: Set to your approved non-care/operations value per gateway policy (do not use \u201cpatient care\u201d).\n- Steps:\n  1) Cohort: Pull Conditions with ICD-10 Z94.2 and recorded-date >= 2023-01-01 (paginate). Capture subject.reference and recordedDate. Apply _elements if available.\n  2) Monthly counts: Normalize recordedDate to UTC, derive YYYY-MM, keep the earliest date per patient-month, exclude current partial month. Output Monthly_counts.csv and Grand Total.\n  3) QA sample (3 rows): Verify Ellen Hernandez cohort membership; choose Ellen + 2 random distinct patients (document RNG seed). For each, fetch Patient (name, MRN) and latest final vital sign. Output QA_sample.csv with exactly the five specified columns.\n  4) Validation: Run the checklist you included (ISO-8601 timestamps, units present, MRN format, Ellen present, exactly 3 rows).\n  5) Audit/log: Record approvals, RNG seed, run timestamp (UTC), counts, exclusions, code version, FHIR base, and POU setting. Store alongside outputs.\n  6) Distribution: Send via the approved secure channel to program leads only.\n\nIf you share:\n- Due time and recipient list, I can finalize the email text accordingly.\n- Your gateway\u2019s PurposeOfUse header name/value and auth pattern, I can tailor the script scaffold.\n- Any local BP/vitals selection rule, I can fold it into the instructions to avoid downstream ambiguity.",
