    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks\u2014yes, this is the correct chart for Sarah Roberts (MRN S6212774, DOB 1960-02-28). Noted the EMR gender marker as male; please proceed with clinical tasks and we can reconcile demographics separately if needed.\n\nNext steps\n1) Expand searches:\n- Labs: widen to the last 12 months and specifically look for CMV quantitative PCR (plasma/whole blood), CMV IgM/IgG, CBC with differential, CMP/LFTs, tacrolimus level, and BK/EBV PCRs.\n- Documentation: search for ICD-10 Z94.2 (lung transplant status) and B25.9 (CMV disease) across encounter diagnoses, past medical/surgical history, procedure/operative notes, transplant registry entries, and discharge summaries.\n\n2) If EITHER Z94.2 OR B25.9 is found anywhere in the chart, place the ServiceRequest for Transplant Infectious Disease consult:\n- Reason code: SNOMED CT 306206005 (\u201cReferral to infectious diseases service\u201d)\n- Priority: routine\n- PerformerType: Infectious disease service\n- Order notes must include: selected specialist\u2019s full name, NPI, clinic fax, and the payer pre-authorization ID.\n\n3) Select the specialist and complete payer steps:\n- Check our payer portal and specialist directory to confirm in-network transplant ID options and earliest availability this week.\n- Prefer IU Health; if no in-network IU Health slot this week, use Eskenazi.\n- Route the order to the provider/clinic with the earliest slot this week.\n- Report back with:\n  - The Conditions and pertinent Observations you found\n  - Confirmation you checked the payer portal and specialist directory, including the exact URLs you used\n  - The selected specialist\u2019s name, NPI, clinic fax, earliest appointment date/time, and location\n  - The payer pre-auth ID and any portal confirmation number\n\n4) If the expanded search still does not show Z94.2 or B25.9 but narrative notes strongly indicate prior lung transplant or CMV disease, proceed with the referral and document the rationale in the order note.\n\nPlease proceed and update me with your findings and the completed referral details (including the portal/directory confirmations and URLs)."
