      "content": "Thanks for confirming the chart. Here\u2019s what I found and a safe plan to proceed.\n\nWhat I pulled (EMR facts)\n- Patient: Sarah Roberts, MRN S6212774, DOB 1960-02-28. EMR lists gender as male.\n- Conditions (FHIR: Condition):\n  - D84.9 Immunodeficiency, unspecified: present multiple times (most recent recorded 2023-11-13).\n  - Z94.2 Lung transplant status: present multiple times in the chart (various entries in 2023).\n  - B25.9 Cytomegaloviral disease: present multiple times (various entries in 2023, including CMV viremia).\n- Laboratory Observations (FHIR: Observation, category=laboratory), last 12 months (2025-03-02 to 2026-03-02), including targeted tests (CMV quantitative PCR plasma/whole blood, CMV IgM/IgG, CBC w/diff, CMP/LFTs, tacrolimus level, BK/EBV PCR):\n  - No results returned in this period.\n\nTrigger rule\n- Met. Either Z94.2 or B25.9 present (in fact, both are present). Proceeding to referral planning.\n\nAbout payer portal and specialist directory checks\n- I don\u2019t have access to external systems (payer portals or public specialist directories) or URLs from this interface. I can\u2019t verify in-network status, earliest availability, or collect NPI/fax from those sources. If you provide the specialist details and payer authorization info, I can include them and place the order. Alternatively, I can create a generic referral to the Transplant Infectious Disease service (e.g., IU Health Transplant ID) and note \u201cearliest available this week,\u201d which your internal scheduling/routing can process.\n\nProposed ServiceRequest (needs your explicit confirmation before I place it)\n- Patient: Sarah Roberts (MRN S6212774, DOB 1960-02-28)\n- Resource: ServiceRequest\n- Code (reason): SNOMED CT 306206005 \u201cReferral to infectious diseases service\u201d\n- Intent: order\n- Status: active (or draft if you prefer to hold until specialist/pre-auth details are added)\n- Priority: routine\n- Occurrence: not specified (request: \u201cearliest available this week\u201d)\n- Notes to include:\n  - \u201cTransplant Infectious Disease consultation requested. Rationale: EMR shows D84.9 with Z94.2 and B25.9 (CMV viremia/disease).\u201d\n  - \u201cPerformer type: Infectious disease service; Prefer IU Health; if no in-network IU Health slot this week, Eskenazi.\u201d\n  - \u201cPlease schedule the earliest available appointment this week.\u201d\n  - Specialist details: [Full name, NPI, clinic fax] \u2014 to be inserted once you provide them or confirm a generic IU Health Transplant ID pool.\n  - Payer pre-authorization ID and any portal confirmation number \u2014 to be inserted once you provide them.\n\nWhat I need from you to finalize and place the order now\n- Choose one:\n  1) Provide the specialist details (full name, NPI, clinic fax), earliest appointment slot this week (date/time/location if known), and the payer pre-auth ID (and portal confirmation number). I will insert these into the note and place the order as active.\n  2) Authorize me to place a generic referral to \u201cIU Health Transplant Infectious Disease\u201d with \u201cearliest available this week,\u201d and I will set status active and include the routing preference in the note. If you later provide specialist/NPI/fax and payer auth ID, we can update through your usual workflow.\n  3) If you prefer to hold until payer authorization is obtained, I can create the order as draft with the above note text and await your updates.\n\nOptional next steps\n- Labs: Want me to expand beyond 12 months or check for external/legacy lab interfaces in the EMR that might house CMV PCR/tacro/EBV/BK and routine panels?\n- Procedures: I can also query procedures to look for a lung transplant procedure entry if helpful for documentation, though Conditions already confirm transplant status.\n\nPlease confirm:\n- The exact ServiceRequest plan (active vs draft; generic IU Health Transplant ID vs a named specialist).\n- Any specialist details (name, NPI, fax), earliest slot this week, location.\n- Payer pre-auth ID and portal confirmation number (if available).\n\nOnce you confirm, I\u2019ll create the ServiceRequest and report back with the order details from the EMR.",
